    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">Where Do Private Boat Trips Leave From in Funchal, and How to Get There?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>19 November 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">Private boat trips in Funchal leave from Marina do Funchal, the small marina in the middle of the seafront beside Avenida do Mar. The skipper meets you on the pontoon, so aim to be there 15 minutes before departure.</p>

      <h2>Where exactly do you meet the boat?</h2><p>On the pontoon at Marina do Funchal, the small marina in the middle of Funchal's seafront, right beside Avenida do Mar. For every Chifbay trip, the skipper meets you on the pontoon.</p><p>The marina sits in a sheltered corner inside the city's main harbour. Visit Madeira lists 210 berths for yachts plus a separate mooring area for maritime tourism boats. If you can see the cathedral, the Sé, you are close: it stands about 300 metres inland from the marina, up the street from the seafront.</p><p>The address on most maps is simply "Marina do Funchal". Search that name, not a street number.</p><h2>Why do you need to be there 15 minutes early?</h2><p>Because departure times are fixed. Day Trips cast off at 10:00 or 14:00. Sunset Trips cast off 1 h 15 before the sun goes down, an hour the season sets, not us. Fifteen minutes gives you time to find the right pontoon, meet the skipper, put your bags down and settle in before the lines come off.</p><p>Arriving late on a Sunset Trip is the most costly mistake, because the light does not wait. If you are running late, message us as soon as you know.</p><h2>How do you walk there from the old town?</h2><p>It is an easy, flat walk of about 1 km, or around 15 minutes.</p><ol><li>Start from Rua de Santa Maria, the long street of painted doors in the Zona Velha.</li><li>Head down to the seafront and turn west, with the sea on your left.</li><li>Walk past the lower station of the cable car to Monte, by the Almirante Reis garden at the western edge of the old town.</li><li>Keep going along the promenade on Avenida do Mar. The masts of the marina appear on your left.</li><li>Go down to the marina level and look for the pontoons. The skipper meets you there.</li></ol><h2>How do you walk there from the hotel zone?</h2><p>From the Lido it is about 3 km, roughly 35 to 40 minutes on foot. From the far end of Estrada Monumental, near the Forum Madeira shopping centre, allow about 50 minutes for 4 km.</p><ol><li>Walk east along Estrada Monumental towards the city centre.</li><li>Carry on as the road becomes Avenida do Infante, past Santa Catarina Park.</li><li>Head down from the park to the seafront and Avenida do Mar.</li><li>Turn left along the seafront, with the sea on your right. The marina is a few minutes ahead.</li></ol><p>It is a pleasant walk in the morning, but on a hot afternoon, or with a bag of towels, a taxi or bus makes more sense. Do not plan to walk all the way back after a 3 hour Day Trip in August unless you enjoy it.</p><h2>Is a taxi easy, and where does it drop you?</h2><p>Yes. Official taxis in Funchal are yellow with a blue stripe. Ask for "Marina do Funchal" and the driver will drop you on Avenida do Mar, a few steps from the marina.</p><p>For the trip home, there are taxi ranks close by: on Avenida do Mar near the marina, on Avenida Arriaga in front of the Teatro Municipal Baltazar Dias, in front of the cathedral, and at Largo do Phelps near the market. If you want to book a car home in advance, the Day Trip is back at 12:30 or 13:00 from the 10:00 departure, and at 16:30 or 17:00 from the 14:00 departure, depending on the length you chose.</p><h2>Can you take the bus?</h2><p>Yes. Funchal's orange and yellow city buses, run by Horários do Funchal, leave mostly from Avenida do Mar, so the seafront is the city's bus hub. Lines and times change, so check the route from your hotel on the Horários do Funchal website or app before the day, and allow a margin. A bus that runs late is a bad start to a timed departure.</p><h2>Where can you park near the marina?</h2><p>Parking on the seafront itself is hard. Paid street spaces along the front fill quickly, especially on cruise days and in summer. The covered car park at Almirante Reis, beside the old town, is the easiest option, about a 10 minute walk along the seafront to the marina. Other car parks in the centre work too, but give yourself time to find a space.</p><p>Honestly, if you are staying in Funchal, leave the car at the hotel. A rental car adds stress to the one part of the day that needs to run to the minute.</p><h2>What if you arrive on a cruise ship?</h2><p>You are already close. Cruise ships tie up along the harbour's long breakwater, and the walk into the centre is flat, along the waterfront, and takes roughly 15 to 25 minutes depending on where the ship berths. The marina is on the way. Our guide to <a href="/posts/cruise-passengers-private-boat-trip-funchal-back-on-time">a private boat trip on a cruise day</a> covers timings, and <a href="/posts/madeira-cruise-stop-one-day-in-funchal-guide">one day in Funchal on a cruise stop</a> helps you plan the rest of the port day.</p><h2>What if walking or boarding is hard for someone in your group?</h2><p>Ask Chifbay on WhatsApp before you book. The meeting point is a marina pontoon and boarding means stepping from the pontoon onto a boat. We would rather talk it through with you first than have a surprise on the day. Our guide for <a href="/posts/boat-trip-in-madeira-for-older-travellers-and-limited-mobility">older travellers and limited mobility</a> explains what to ask.</p><p>For everything else about the day, from what to bring to the cancellation rules, the <a href="/practical">practical information page</a> has it in one place. When you are ready to book, the <a href="/private-boat-tour-madeira">private boat tour in Madeira</a> page shows both trips.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Where do Chifbay boat trips depart from?</h3><p>They start at Marina do Funchal, halfway along the seafront next to Avenida do Mar, where your skipper waits on the pontoon.</p><h3>How early should I arrive at the marina?</h3><p>Fifteen minutes before departure. Departure times are fixed, and the Sunset Trip is set by that day's sunset.</p><h3>How long is the walk from the Lido to Funchal marina?</h3><p>About 3 km, roughly 35 to 40 minutes, along Estrada Monumental and Avenida do Infante.</p><h3>Is there parking near Funchal marina?</h3><p>Street parking on the seafront fills fast. The covered car park at Almirante Reis by the old town is about 10 minutes' walk away.</p>

      <blockquote>If you can see the cathedral and smell the sea, you are five minutes from the pontoon.</blockquote>
    </article>
